;; The moment at a call's return (queue 297; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 297"): CPython's reference counting
;; frees a generator a call leaves suspended when the call drops its last reference (next(gen()), any(gen())): its
;; close then (GeneratorExit thrown in, finally blocks and a monitor's events), its frame's locals with it. pyi knows that
;; moment without a collection when the generator's only holder was the value stack: made by the calling frame's
;; previous instruction (stampGen: the frame's address and instruction, and callSeq, every call counting itself, so no
;; call ran between), not handed out since (f_generator marks it exposed), and the last argument of a consumer that
;; keeps no reference to its arguments (Builtin.dropsArg: next, any, all, min, max, sum, sorted). No instruction ran
;; between its making and the consumer's call, so nothing stored it; the consumer kept nothing; its own frame does not
;; hold it (a frame object does not keep its generator alive in CPython either). dropGen closes it at the return. Cost:
;; an increment per call and a flag test per built-in call; a collection only for its frame's locals with a finalizer
;; due (222's moment, as del's).


